WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.405
MUTXRI Terminal.

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:12.810
Financial data built for research: 938 listed securities across Johannesburg, Lagos, Nairobi and Cairo, with statements and filings behind every one.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:21.430
The terminal asks you to sign in: continue with Google, or create an account with an email address and a password of at least eight characters.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:32.720
Inside, the workspace is a set of windows: the watchlist, the panel stage with its tab row, the popup window, the market window and the chat room, with the tape across the top.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:40.920
The tape carries the index levels first, then every listed security and its move on the day, in the exchange's own ticker codes.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:47.490
The watchlist holds every company on the board with its ticker, price and change, and narrows as you type.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:57.040
Click a security and the market window opens it: price, volume, sector, the chief executive, competitors, customers and shareholders.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:03.365
One window now carries both: the market sheet, then the research stack.

00:01:03.365 --> 00:01:09.330
Price history, valuation, growth, quality and risk, key statistics, ratios and audit flags.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:17.160
With no security chosen, the market window shows the board: how many names are up and down, the tone of the session, the top gainers, losers and the most active.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:22.545
The terminal is a command line as well as a mouse.

00:01:22.545 --> 00:01:27.730
HELP lists every panel code it carries, from heatmap and screener to bonds, FX, macro and portfolio.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:33.005
A ticker alone opens the security.

00:01:33.005 --> 00:01:37.970
A ticker with a function opens that function on it: SCOM FIN opens Safaricom's financials in the centre panel.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:43.140
Markets switch by name.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:47.960
Type CAIRO and the finder offers the board; take it and the terminal reloads on the EGX, priced in Egyptian pounds.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:56.740
Cairo, the EGX: the last close in Egyptian pounds, with the heatmap sizing each sector by weight and colouring it by the day's move.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:06.120
Click a sector for its securities, then a name for the chart: candles, line or area, over any timeframe from a single day to the full history.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:15.460
The screener filters the whole board by sector, price, change, volume and yield, runs the filter and exports the result to CSV.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:25.910
Announcements carries the NSE filings wire, and a dividend calendar built from the dated notices: dividends, payments and book closures, month by month.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:34.460
News merges the press headlines, the regulator wire and corporate actions into one feed, with the source and the date on every item.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:43.180
Bonds and treasury bills: central-bank auction results for all four markets, each with its auction date, and a blank where the source has no figure.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:53.200
Foreign exchange: a converter and a triangulated cross-rate grid, the shilling, naira, rand and Egyptian pound against the dollar, euro and sterling.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:03:02.260
Macro: consumer price inflation for the four markets, each value the published annual figure with its year, plotted from the World Bank series.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:07.155
Paper trading fills orders at the last close.

00:03:07.155 --> 00:03:11.670
Type a ticker and a quantity, watch the ticket price the order before it goes in, then place it.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:19.910
The paper book takes orders at the last close, in this browser only.

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:27.780
Two of them placed here, then valued in the portfolio: exposure by sector and by exchange as donuts, profit and loss per position, the book value curve and the risk per position.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:34.135
Settings carry the theme colour, the interface font, the default market you land on and the preferences for the command bar and notifications.

00:03:34.135 --> 00:03:40.110
Invite a friend and your own link is copied to the clipboard.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:51.690
Compare puts two companies side by side: price, valuation, profitability and growth, with the stronger figure on each line marked, so the better business is visible at a glance.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:04:03.570
Financials shows the income statement, balance sheet and cash flow exactly as the company filed them, with reporting periods side by side, and a blank where the filing does not state a figure.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:12.500
The written guide documents every window, panel and command, with the source behind each figure and the gaps stated where the data does not exist.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.930
MUTXRI Terminal.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:16.060
Every African market, one terminal.

